                  <provenance>Label at foot of spine ‘M 242’, the number 2862 inside front cover; cutting from a sale catalogue, and 'no IV' at head, fol. i recto. An 18th-century note on fol. ii recto refers to MS. 1129 in archbishop Laud's collection (i.e. MS. Laud Misc. 733, with the Middle English translation of the <title>Tractatus de armis </title>) and wrongly infers, as does the sale description, that the present manuscript was once in Laud's collection.</provenance>
